  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, and we've established that multi-profile + avgpool is the strongest RNA-only setting. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA n2000), leaving uncertainty about whether a learned representation could further improve performance. Question: config_005 (RNA, multi-profile, scvi_n200, avgpool) changes only the RNA encoder relative to config_002, cleanly isolating the encoder effect while holding profile setting and aggregation constant. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly tests whether the linear PCA representation is a bottleneck or whether a non-linear learned embedding (scVI) captures additional biological signal. If scvi outperforms PCA, it justifies investing further in learned encoders (including scgpt) and multimodal fusion with richer RNA features. If it underperforms, it confirms PCA is sufficient and redirects budget toward fusion strategy or image modality questions. This single-variable comparison maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
